2022 has been a tough year but it's been  especially tough for one group of  americans the middle class has gotten  absolutely squeezed they've lost more  than the people who make more than them  they've saved less than the people who  make less than them and they're being  hit the hardest by inflation  how did this happen  i'm going to walk you through the  financial data that show how the middle  class is feeling the squeeze  first just who makes up the middle class  the federal reserve classifies american  households into six income categories  and the middle class is made up of the  groups in the middle of u.s income  distribution that's households that earn  about forty eight thousand dollars to  about one hundred twenty seven thousand  dollars a year data show this group is  getting hit hardest by just about  everything new research from bank of  america found that middle-class  americans were seeing prices rise by 9.4  in may from a year before versus an 8.6  inflation rate for all americans  that's the highest rate for all income  groups and it's largely because folks in  the middle class spend a larger share of  their income on driving and auto  expenses and those costs have  skyrocketed the middle class has lost  the biggest share of its assets in the  stock market the loss has been larger  than even the top one percent of  households which own more than half of  all equity and mutual fund shares  according to federal reserve data so  even though middle-class households own  less stocks they lost a bigger  percentage of what they do have in the  first quarter downturn fed data also  showed that the middle class is taking  on more debt households earning between  75 and 127 000  now hold the most consumer credit debt  of all groups  outpacing even households that earn  twice as much or more and data from  moody's investor service shows those  upper middle income americans have less  savings than every group except the  lowest income americans and they reduced  their savings in the fourth quarter of  2021 and the first quarter of 2022 by  more than any other group  so why did this happen economists at  moody's say it's largely result of these  middle-class households being excluded  from stimulus checks and income-based  tax credits  many also lost their jobs during the  pandemic and received unemployment  benefits that were less than their  previous wages  with lockdowns ending and prices rising  they've eaten into their savings and  taken on debt to keep up with purchases  wages for the middle class are  increasing but well below the rate of  inflation meaning these households are  losing money every month  only the lowest income households are  seeing wage gains that are above  inflation according to calculations by  economist aaron dube  the bottom line is the middle class got  squeezed to start the year and with  inflation still hot and markets  continuing to struggle  there's no sign this squeeze will be  short  we heard az tell us on nasa's classic  album illmatic that he was visualizing  the realism of life in actuality forget  who's the baddest a person's status  depends on salary and my mentality is  money orientated i'm destined to live  the dream for all my peeps who never  made it  that's all for now see you next time
 

